abstract: >-
  Software for NV-diamond quantum magnetometers built with coding agents:
  a physics simulator, INT8 edge machine learning, PID plus neural-network
  control on a PolarFire SoC FPGA, a field-vector tracker, a demo dashboard,
  and a workbench that checks written claims with local language-model critics.
  Current validation limits: this project has no live NV-diamond measurement
  setup. FPGA tests used replayed synthetic spectra. Separate software studies
  used public measured NV datasets, but incomplete reference labels, calibration
  records, and independent acquisitions limited the conclusions. The FPGA
  control path and model inference ran on a development kit with replayed
  input. These parts are not one integrated sensing system. Reliable sensing
  and a useful neural advantage over strong classical methods remain unproven.
